pressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. "}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn5le18ob04re1img01.png"}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you hear in a workplace."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Review - Long Vowel Sounds"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "There are rules for the long vowel sound."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Explanation\\t\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Rule 1\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" When a word has <span class=\\\"strong\\\">two</span> vowels, usually you pronounce the name  of the <span class=\\\"strong\\\">first</span>  vowel and the <span class=\\\"strong\\\">second</span> vowel is silent. <br/> Exceptions: <span class=\\\"italic\\\">could</span>, <span class=\\\"italic\\\">country</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> cheese<br/> treat<br/> fruit<br/> roast </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Rule 2\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" If a vowel is followed by  <span class=\\\"strong\\\">w</span> or  <span class=\\\"strong\\\">y</span>, you usually say the vowel with a  <span class=\\\"underline\\\">long vowel sound</span>.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> show<br/> brown<br/> pay<br/> blew  </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Rule 3\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"If a word has <span class=\\\"strong\\\">one</span> vowel and it comes at the end of the word, you usually use a <span class=\\\"underline\\\">long vowel sound</span>.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <span class=\\\"italic\\\">he<br/> me<br/> go<br/> try<span class=\\\"italic\\\">\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Rule 4 \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" If a word has a vowel and a consonant that is followed by <span class=\\\"strong\\\">e</span>, the <span class=\\\"strong\\\">e</span> is usually silent. However, it makes the vowel before it <span class=\\\"underline\\\">long</span>. <br/>Exceptions: <span class=\\\"italic\\\">gone</span>, <span class=\\\"italic\\\">have</span>, <span class=\\\"italic\\\">live</span>, <span class=\\\"italic\\\">come</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> plane<br/> bone<br/> bake </span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "brie"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a type of soft cheese "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": " (noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The baked brie appetizer sounds delicious."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le18ob04aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "in for a treat"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " about to have something special "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": " (expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We are in for a treat tonight!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le18ob04aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "lamb shanks "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a slow cooked roast lamb dish "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun):  "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We are having lamb shanks for dinner."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le18ob04aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "cliff hanger "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a stressful, exciting situation"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": " (expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The end of the television show is a cliff hanger."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le18ob04aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "buffet "}, {"type": "definition", "content": " a piece of dining room furniture "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The plates and napkins are in the buffet."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le18ob04aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "police officer "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a person whose job is to enforce laws, investigate crimes, and make arrests  "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The police officer was in the hospital."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le18ob04aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "specialty"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "something that a person or place is known for making or producing very well"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": " (noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": " Example: This is a specialty at work."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le18ob04aud07"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "fridge "}, {"type": "definition", "content": " a cold place to store food "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: There are some drinks and a cheesecake in the fridge."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le18ob04aud08"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Write a 10-line dialogue about you making dinner for a friend."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Chat about jobs and work."}, {"type": "text", "content": "What are you going to make?"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Who is setting the table?"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Use at least 10 words with a long vowel sound."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Read the dialogue aloud with a partner."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I write a dialogue about spending time with a friend."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I use at least 10 words with the long vowel sound."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I read my dialogue aloud about jobs and work."}]}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"_data": [], "template_override": 1, "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "id": 0}, {"id": 1, "type": "audio", "title": "", "_data": [], "template_override": 1, "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"audiosrc": "engenn5le18ob04re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn5le18ob04re2img05.jpg", "images": [{"text": "", "id": 0, "time": "0", "image": "engenn5le18ob04re2img05.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: You guys are in for a treat tonight!<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: That's right! We have a chef in the house. It smells fantastic in the kitchen. <br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Vanessa, what are you making?<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: I'd thought we would start with some baked brie cheese with apple slices.", "id": 1, "time": "100", "image": "engenn5le18ob04re2img05.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: That sounds delicious! It's nice to have great dinner after a long day at work.<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Then, you will be served lamb shanks with roasted vegetables. It's a specialty at work.<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: I can't wait! Peter can you help me set the table? The napkins are in the buffet drawer.", "id": 2, "time": "14000", "image": "engenn5le18ob04re2img01.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: Alright. Would you ladies like a drink? <br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Sure, I'd love a soft drink.<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Me too, thanks. There's some in the fridge.", "id": 3, "time": "31500", "image": "engenn5le18ob04re2img02.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: Remember, I brought that cheesecake for dessert. <br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Hey Sal,  <span class=\"italic\">Boston Nights</span> is on later tonight. The last episode was such a cliff hanger\u2026.I can't wait! <br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Oh, Jake, the police officer is still in the hospital.<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: You two love that show! How about I join you?", "id": 4, "time": "39500", "image": "engenn5le18ob04re2img02.jpg"}]}}]}], "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}]}], "id": 0, "type": "scholar", "exercises": [{"questions": [], "stimuli_ids": [0], "id": 0, "type": "WLC", "img_path": "", "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about rooms and objects in them."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "  I can use and pronounce the long vowel sounds. "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can identify key information in a short audio."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " Do you like to cook for your friends? "}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " Your family? What is your favorite dish?"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}]}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "correct_feedback": "Correct", "attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have 2 tries"}, {"type": "text", "content": "you have 1 attempt left"}], "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "try again"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time"}]}}, {"type": "free_header_text", "content": " Ask your partner:"}, {"type": "free_type_text_area", "content": "Pronunciation Spot: What's cooking? "}], "template_override": 1}, {"questions"